<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>
    This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
    San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser sends technical data to GitHub's
    servers, including your IP address, the requested page, the time and your browser's user agent.
    GitHub logs the IP address for security purposes, even if you do not have a GitHub account.
    We cannot see these logs and have no influence on how long GitHub keeps them.
</p>
<p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. We have a legitimate interest in delivering this website securely
    and reliably. GitHub is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, which covers the transfer to
    the USA (Art. 45 GDPR). Details: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter</h2>
<p>
    When you sign up on the home page, we store the email address you enter. We use it only to tell you
    about DevFest Berlin: for example when tickets go on sale, the Call for Speakers opens, or speakers are
    announced.
</p>
<p>
    The sign-up form sends your address to Google Forms, a service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House,
    Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. The addresses are stored in a Google spreadsheet that only the
    organizers can access. Google may also process the data in the USA. Google LLC is certified under the
    EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (Art. 45 GDPR). Details: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
</p>
<p>
    Legal basis: your consent, Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR. You can withdraw it at any time with effect for the
    future: reply to any of our emails or write to {{ contactLink(site.contactEmail) }}, and we will
    delete your address. We delete the whole list at the latest 12 months after the event.
</p>

<h2>Contacting us by email</h2>
<p>
    If you email us, we use your address and message only to answer you. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR
    if your message relates to taking part in the event, otherwise Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. We delete the
    correspondence when it is no longer needed.
</p>

<h2 id="code-of-conduct-reports">Code of Conduct reports</h2>
<p>
    If you report a concern under our <a href="/code-of-conduct/">Code of Conduct</a>, we record what you tell
    us, your contact details if you give them, and the names of the people involved. We use this only to deal
    with the report. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR, our legitimate interest in a safe event for everyone.
</p>
<p>
    Only the organizers handling the report see it. Where needed to act, we may share the necessary details
    with venue security, the police, or Google's community team, which runs the Google Developer Groups
    program. We delete report records at the latest 12 months after the event, unless we need them longer
    to resolve a case.
</p>

<h2>Tickets, talk submissions and other platforms</h2>
<p>
    Links to the ticket shop, the Call for Speakers and our social media profiles lead to other providers.
    Nothing is sent to them until you click a link. From then on, their privacy policies apply.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
    <li>have it corrected (Art. 16) or deleted (Art. 17)</li>
    <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18)</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21)</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time (Art. 7 (3))</li>
</ul>
<p>To use any of these rights, write to {{ contactLink(site.contactEmail) }}.</p>
<p>
    You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The authority
    responsible for us is the Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit, Alt-Moabit 59-61,
    10555 Berlin, <a href="https://www.datenschutz-berlin.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener">datenschutz-berlin.de</a>.
</p>

